README for RTAPI

RTAPI is the LinuxCNC abstraction used by realtime and non-realtime code.
This reduced tree supports the POSIX uspace backend only. Realtime modules
are built as shared objects and loaded by rtapi_app.

Primary files:

rtapi.h             public RTAPI declarations
rtapi_app.h         realtime module entry declarations
rtapi_common.h      internal RTAPI typedefs and shared data
rtapi_proc.h        legacy /proc support declarations
uspace_common.h     uspace scheduling and environment helpers
uspace_posix.cc     POSIX realtime implementation
uspace_rtapi_app.cc rtapi_app process support
uspace_rtapi_main.cc rtapi_app main entrypoint
uspace_ulapi.c      user-level API implementation

Build outline:

1. Run configure with the uspace backend:

   ./configure --with-realtime=uspace

2. Build LinuxCNC:

   make

The generated Makefile installs realtime modules below the configured
LinuxCNC realtime module directory. A run-in-place build uses ../rtlib.

Runtime outline:

1. linuxcnc starts scripts/realtime.
2. scripts/realtime reads rtapi.conf and checks the POSIX uspace runtime.
3. rtapi_app loads realtime module shared objects from the configured module
   path.
4. HAL and motion components allocate shared memory through RTAPI and expose
   their pins, parameters, and functions through HAL.

On non-PREEMPT_RT kernels the POSIX backend may run without hard realtime
latency guarantees. The build still uses the same uspace backend; the kernel
only changes the scheduling behavior available at runtime.
